Z||000000||Roy||12-26-1999||02:40 AM||||I need some help people.....On the drive down to my folks house for xmas the retainer clip on one of the cables broke(dunno if its the selector or the other one) I can see where it should be. But right now I only have 2nd and 4th gear without that clip. I need to know if any of you can think of something I can rig up to get home 40 miles because I gotta get to work monday and the dealership isn't open sunday, and I dbout the autoparts store has the clips. There like $2 clips LOL and its keeping my car from backing out of the driveway. Any ideas would be appreciated. Or if anyone has any extra of these clips and is willing to sell them too me and there anywhere near portland oregon. <P>Thanks In Advance<P>Roy<P>ps: sorry for the bad grammer its late :P||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||12-26-1999||07:31 AM||||Since you don't need to go too far and hopefully not too many gear changes, you might try using several rubber bands or old underwear waist band elastic (etc.) to rig up the shift cable temporarily. It probably won't last long before it slips back out, but maybe with some luck and only having to stop to redo it a couple times, you can make it back home.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Wolfhound||12-26-1999||07:40 AM||||Might try securing it in some manner with  screw clamps.||||reg||1
Z||000003||TOM||12-26-1999||02:06 PM||||A heater hose size clamp will work great.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||12-26-1999||02:46 PM||||Nylon cable ties? (Radio Shack, Home Depot, etc.)||||reg||1
Z||000005||HotFieroGT||12-26-1999||10:32 PM||||I don't know about you guys, but I have a ton of of underwear that are shot except for the waistbands.  Thanks to Batboy I have finally figured out a use for them!||||reg||12
